      <b><span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">بَيِّعٌ</span></b> : see <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">بَائِعٌ</span>, in five places. ― 
       <p class="alpheios-lex-sense-separator"> </p><span class="alpheios-lex-sense-spacer2"> </span>-b2-  Also A man
<i>who sells,</i> or <i>buys, well;</i> and so ↓ <b><span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">بَيُوعٌ</span></b> : fem. of
the former with <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">ة</span>: pl. mase. <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">بَيِّعُونَ</span>, and pl. fem.
<span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">بَيِّعَاتٌ</span>; neither the masc. nor the fem. having a
broken pl. (TA.)

